{"type":"message","id":"19e9273f","parentId":"bd40f7ce","timestamp":"2026-05-18T08:06:44.323Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I’m pulling the top items from multiple feeds now, then I’ll cross-check for one story that’s clearly shared and published today."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1XgSe632qaM0U4dAs9EsndQy","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport urllib.request, ssl, xml.etree.ElementTree as ET, re\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfeeds = {\n 'CoinDesk':'https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/',\n 'CoinTelegraph':'https://cointelegraph.com/rss',\n 'GoogleNews':'https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=bitcoin+crypto&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en'\n}\nctx = ssl.create_default_context()\nfor name,url in feeds.items():\n    print(f'\\n## {name}')\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=20, context=ctx) as r:\n        data = r.read()\n    root = ET.fromstring(data)\n    # RSS 2.0 items\n    items = root.findall('./channel/item')[:10]\n    for i,it in enumerate(items,1):\n        title = (it.findtext('title') or '').strip()\n        link = (it.findtext('link') or '').strip()\n        pub = (it.findtext('pubDate') or it.findtext('{http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/}date') or '').strip()\n        desc = (it.findtext('description') or '').strip()\n        desc = re.sub('<[^>]+>',' ',desc)\n        print(f'{i}. {pub}\\n   {title}\\n   {link}\\n   {desc[:220]}')\nPY","workdir":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher","timeout":60}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_Z2PA0e0rDxK1QA6IRTdtQXZm","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport urllib.request, ssl, xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\nfrom collections import Counter\nfeeds = ['https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/','https://cointelegraph.com/rss','https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=bitcoin+crypto&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en']\nctx = ssl.create_default_context()\nfor url in feeds:\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=20, context=ctx) as r:\n        root = ET.fromstring(r.read())\n    print('\\nFEED', url)\n    for it in root.findall('./channel/item')[:5]:\n        print('-', (it.findtext('title') or '').strip())\nPY","workdir":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4-mini","usage":{"input":1700,"output":790,"cacheRead":11392,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13882,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779091598600,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DgnHmEcjjFkA7kLIcObE6ofMSKQmV"}}
{"type":"message","id":"b52e581a","parentId":"19e9273f","timestamp":"2026-05-18T08:06:45.665Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_1XgSe632qaM0U4dAs9EsndQy","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## CoinDesk\n1. Mon, 18 May 2026 07:13:08 +0000\n   Crypto security is turning into an AI arms race as agents may overwhelm compliance teams\n   https://www.coindesk.com/tech/2026/05/18/crypto-security-is-turning-into-an-ai-arms-race-as-agents-may-overwhelm-compliance-teams\n   AI agents and automated payments could reach a scale that crypto monitoring systems built for human-paced markets cannot handle, Elliptic CEO Simone Maini warned.\n2. Mon, 18 May 2026 07:05:20 +0000\n   Aave restores ether borrowing limits after $230 million exploit\n   https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/aave-restores-weth-collateral-limits-as-rseth-crisis-enters-recovery-phase\n   The DeFi lending protocol reversed restrictions imposed after April’s $292 million exploit, restoring borrowing capacity across six networks as contagion fears ease.\n3. Mon, 18 May 2026 06:55:50 +0000\n   Bitcoin Depot, North America's largest bitcoin ATM operator, files for bankruptcy\n   https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/bitcoin-depot-once-north-america-s-largest-bitcoin-atm-operator-files-for-bankruptcy\n   Bitcoin Depot, the largest bitcoin ATM operator in North America and publicly listed on Nasdaq, has filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy.\n4. Mon, 18 May 2026 06:47:37 +0000\n   Iran may be turning the Strait of Hormuz into a bitcoin-based insurance market, local reports say\n   https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/iran-may-be-turning-the-strait-of-hormuz-into-a-bitcoin-insurance-market-local-reports-say\n   State-linked Fars News reported that Iran’s economy ministry has been working on a plan to manage shipping through the Strait with payments in bitcoin.\n5. Mon, 18 May 2026 05:47:13 +0000\n   Crypto traders betting on a rally lose $563 million in liquidations. Ether and bitcoin suffer the most\n   https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/crypto-traders-betting-on-a-rally-lose-usd563-million-in-liquidations-ether-and-bitcoin-suffer-the-most\n   Ether and bitcoin led liquidations, as their prices dropped on macroeconomic concerns.\n6. Mon, 18 May 2026 05:01:11 +0000\n   HYPE pops 7%, beating bitcoin declines, as SpaceX pre-IPO lands on Hyperliquid\n   https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/hype-pops-7-beating-bitcoin-declines-as-spacex-pre-ipo-lands-on-hyperliquid\n   Hyperliquid's HYPE token rallied 7% over 24 hours after Trade.xyz launched the first pre-IPO perpetual market on the platform, offering synthetic exposure to SpaceX at a reference valuation of $1.78 trillion.\n7. Mon, 18 May 2026 04:37:06 +0000\n   Yet another crypto bridge falls victim to an $11 million hack\n   https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/yet-another-crypto-bridge-falls-victim-to-an-usd11-million-hack\n   The latest attack adds to growing string of cross-chain infrastructure exploits.\n8. Mon, 18 May 2026 03:52:10 +0000\n   Bitcoin slides under $77,000 as oil shock and Treasury yields hit risk assets\n   https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/bitcoin-slides-under-usd77-000-as-oil-shock-and-treasury-yields-hit-risk-assets\n   Long-term holders are still sitting tight and exchange balances remain near six-year lows, Binance Research data shows, but underwater short-term holders leave BTC vulnerable to macro shocks.\n9. Sun, 17 May 2026 18:30:00 +0000\n   The Clarity Act took a step forward: State of Crypto\n   https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/17/the-clarity-act-took-a-step-forward-state-of-crypto\n   Unpacking Thursday's at-times contentious markup hearing.\n10. Sun, 17 May 2026 12:00:00 +0000\n   DeFi's new front: VerifiedX bets bitcoin's next chapter is programmable, private\n   https://www.coindesk.com/tech/2026/05/17/defi-s-new-front-verifiedx-bets-bitcoin-s-next-chapter-is-programmable-private\n   VerifiedX says its Bitcoin sidechain enables programmable, privacy-preserving transactions without synthetic wrappers, targeting growing institutional demand for native DeFi on the original blockchain system.\n\n## CoinTelegraph\n1. Mon, 18 May 2026 07:02:06 +0000\n   Surging oil prices have been driving Ether selling pressure: Tom Lee\n   https://cointelegraph.com/news/surging-oil-prices-key-driver-of-eth-selling-pressure-says-tom-lee?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\n       Fundstrat's Tom Lee pointed out an inverse correlation between crude and Ether as oil surged back to around $110 on Monday. \n \n2. Mon, 18 May 2026 06:53:38 +0000\n   Reports suggest Iran is mulling Hormuz ‘insurance’ scheme, paid in Bitcoin\n   https://cointelegraph.com/news/iran-mulls-platform-for-ships-transiting-strait-of-hormuz-to-pay-in-bitcoin-report?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\n       Screenshots of a website called “Hormuz Safe” have been circulating on social media, which offers “digital insurance” for ships passing through the Strait of Hormuz. \n3. Mon, 18 May 2026 05:23:11 +0000\n   Senate crypto bill at risk beyond midterms if not passed by August: NYDIG\n   https://cointelegraph.com/news/senate-crypto-bill-august-advance-in-lame-duck-session-nydig?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\n       NYDIG’s Greg Cipolaro says the Senate’s crypto market structure bill is at risk of failing if it cannot clear a floor vote by August.\n \n4. Mon, 18 May 2026 05:06:21 +0000\n   Analysts debate whether Bitcoin is in ‘sell in May’ bear market setup\n   https://cointelegraph.com/news/sell-in-may-historical-pattern-could-see-btc-back-at-33k-analyst?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\n       Some analysts argue that a comparatively broadened, institutionalized buyer base for crypto today may prevent a repeat of the drawdowns seen in May 2018 and May 2022.  \n5. Mon, 18 May 2026 05:02:08 +0000\n   WETH markets return to normal operations on Aave amid rsETH recovery progress\n   https://cointelegraph.com/news/aave-restores-weth-borrowing-after-kelp-dao-rseth-exploit?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\n       Aave applied a temporary freeze to WETH as a precautionary safety measure in response to the Kelp DAO exploit, alongside freezes on the rsETH and wrsETH reserves.  \n6. Mon, 18 May 2026 02:40:22 +0000\n   Grayscale, VanEck amend US spot BNB ETF filings, stepping closer to potential launch\n   https://cointelegraph.com/news/grayscale-vaneck-advance-bnb-etf-filings-for-potential-sec-approval?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\n       The US securities regulator approved 21Shares’ Hyperliquid ETF last week, adding to a growing number of cryptocurrencies converted into ETF wrappers in the US. \n7. Sun, 17 May 2026 22:30:00 +0000\n   Here’s what happened in crypto today\n   https://cointelegraph.com/news/what-happened-in-crypto-today?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\n       Need to know what happened in crypto today? Here is the latest news on daily trends and events impacting Bitcoin price, blockchain, DeFi, NFTs, Web3 and crypto regulation. \n8. Sun, 17 May 2026 21:14:00 +0000\n   Bernstein says Figure's Q1 results shows uniqueness of blockchain marketplaces\n   https://cointelegraph.com/news/bernstein-say-figures-q1-shows-uniqueness-of-blockchain-marketplaces?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\n       Figure Technology Solutions latest quarterly results showed Bernstein analysts how different it is from most balance sheet-based fintech lending platforms. \n9. Sun, 17 May 2026 18:01:00 +0000\n   Saylor signals BTC buy as retail holders get push on STRC dividend vote\n   https://cointelegraph.com/news/saylor-signals-btc-buy-as-retail-holders-get-push-on-strc-dividend-vote?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campai